    "teaserText": "",
    "startText": "[groggy] Anthony woke on a hard wooden bench in a cell, with a pounding headache and a mouth like a camel's backside. Outside, he could hear a crowd cheering.\n\n[concerned] His cellmates were a sorry-looking bunch. One wore a helmet that looked suspiciously like a cooking pot, another had a breastplate held together with rope, and the third had somehow managed to lose one sandal but keep two shoulder guards.\n\n[disgusted] The oldest spat on the floor and shoved a dented shield and a rather rusty gladius into Anthony's hands.\n\n[angry drunk] \"Here you are, lad. The shield still works. The sword... well, hit them with the sharp end.\"\n\n[angry] \"Fortuna audaces iuvat! Fortune favours the brave!\"\n\n[deadpan] Anthony wished fortune would occasionally favour the badly equipped as well.",
